    <data name="BillingTitle" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Questions about paying</value>
    </data>
    <data name="BillingLede" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>The assistant on this page answers the rest. It can tell you how Sumwise works, but it gives no tax advice.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="BillingFaq1Question" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Is the Free plan really free?</value>
    </data>
    <data name="BillingFaq1Answer" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Yes. Three invoices a month, quotes and payment reminders, with no card and no time limit. Move to a paid plan when you need more.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="BillingFaq2Question" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Do you add VAT to the price?</value>
    </data>
    <data name="BillingFaq2Answer" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Prices are shown without VAT unless you switch it on. We charge VAT at your country's standard rate. Businesses with a VAT number in another EU country pay none under the reverse charge; Austrian businesses pay 20%.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="BillingFaq3Question" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Can I change or cancel my plan?</value>
    </data>
    <data name="BillingFaq3Answer" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Any time, in Settings. An upgrade starts at once and you pay only the difference for the rest of the month. A downgrade or a cancellation takes effect at the end of the month.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="BillingFaq4Question" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>How does the money-back guarantee work?</value>
    </data>
    <data name="BillingFaq4Answer" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Write to hello@sumwise.example within 30 days of your first payment. We refund the full amount to the card or account you paid with, within 5 working days.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="BillingFaq5Question" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>What happens to my books if I leave?</value>
    </data>
    <data name="BillingFaq5Answer" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>They're yours. Export everything as PDF and CSV at any time. After you cancel, your account stays readable for 12 months, and then we delete it.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="BillingFaq6Question" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Do I get an invoice for my subscription?</value>
    </data>
    <data name="BillingFaq6Answer" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Every month, by email and in Settings. It's made in Sumwise, of course.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="AboutTitle" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>About Sumwise</value>
    </data>
    <data name="AboutDescription" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Sumwise was started in Vienna in 2021 by a tax accountant and a freelance developer. 31 people now work on it, for about 48,000 freelancers and small businesses.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="AboutLede" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>We make invoicing and bookkeeping software for people who would rather be doing their actual work. 31 of us, in Vienna, for about 48,000 freelancers and small businesses.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="StoryTitle" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>A tax accountant and a freelancer</value>
    </data>
    <data name="StoryBody1" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Clara Weninger spent eleven years as a tax accountant in Vienna. Every spring her freelance clients arrived with the same shoebox of receipts and the same apology.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="StoryBody2" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>In 2021 she started Sumwise with Jonas Petrović, a freelance developer and one of those clients. Their idea was simple: if the invoices, the payments and the receipts already sat in one place, the books would mostly write themselves, and an accountant could check instead of type.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="StoryQuote" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>We don't give tax advice, and we never will. We do the typing, so that you and your accountant can do the thinking.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="StoryQuoteBy" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Clara Weninger, co-founder</value>
    </data>
    <data name="PromisesTitle" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Three things we promise</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Promise1Title" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Your books are yours</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Promise1Body" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Export everything, any time, in formats any accountant can open. Leaving us takes five minutes.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Promise2Title" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>No tax advice in disguise</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Promise2Body" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Sumwise prepares the numbers and shows where each one comes from. The decisions stay with you and your accountant.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Promise3Title" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Prices that don't creep</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Promise3Body" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>We announce any price change 60 days ahead, by email, and never change the price of a month you've already paid for.</value>
    </data>
